  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "At the moment, setting the root for a pickup in Unity with the VRC SDK requires making a game object, and hoping the transforms match what VR Chat needs to make it look natural in the avatar's hand. This oftentimes requires going in and out of VR Chat to make sure things match up the way you want them to. Would love to see an option where you can actually adjust it to fit in the sample avatar's hand in the editor exactly how you want it to fit on any other VRC Avatar, and for it to record those transforms. Makes it more natural to have a visual representation of what the transforms mean.",
